Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 18:16:30 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(app): a lathe thread's spindle arcs are judged by
 radius in the travel check

#631: the built-in Lathe (X 0..320) refused every thread - its passes
are arcs about the spindle axis, whose far side and quarter points read
negative X (the CL's antipode; the spindle turns the work, the slide
never goes there). On a lathe, an XY arc centred on the spindle axis is
now judged in X by its radius; every other move keeps its signed X, so
a real past-centre over-travel is still refused.

Pinned by lathe_thread_travel (2): a thread passes the built-in Lathe
(fails without the fix with the issue's message), and the same thread
on a 0..2 mm X stroke is refused in X.

Fixes #631

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
